course: dictionary
lesson: 1454
title: A noun for a nut
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A noun is a naming word. It names a person, place, thing or idea. «Cashew» is a noun because it names a curved nut, and «cashews» means more than one. When you meet a noun, ask yourself: what is this thing?
explain: The same word can name two different things. «The cashew is also the tree that grows these nuts.» The clue is «grows»: nuts do not grow on their own, but trees do. So here the cashew means the tree, not the nut.
explain: Context also tells you how a food is used or what a word feels like. «Some children are allergic to nuts, so many schools are nut-free.» The sentence shows that cashews can make some children ill, so schools may ban them.
fact: A noun is a naming word for a person, place, thing or idea.
fact: «Cashew» is a noun: you can say «a cashew» or «cashews».
fact: A cashew is a curved, kidney-shaped nut that grows at the bottom of a fruit called the cashew apple.
fact: The cashew is also the name of the tree that grows these nuts.
fact: Cashew trees grow in hot countries such as India, Vietnam, parts of Africa and Brazil.
exercise: «The cashew nut grows under a fleshy cashew apple.» What is a cashew apple? | A kind of cashew nut | A hard shell | A tree trunk | *A fruit that the cashew nut grows under
exercise: «The cashew is also the tree that grows these nuts.» In this sentence, what does cashew mean? | A nut shell | A school snack | *A tree | A hot country
exercise: «Its shell holds an oily liquid that burns skin, so cashews are sold shelled and cooked.» Why are cashews cooked before they are sold? | *Because the shell's oil burns skin | Because they are too small to see | Because they grow only in schools | Because they taste better when they are cold
test: What is a noun? | A word that joins two sentences | *A naming word for a person, place, thing or idea | A word that describes a noun | A word that shows an action
test: «Some children are allergic to nuts, so many schools are nut-free.» What does this suggest? | Nuts are only eaten in hot countries | *Some nuts could make some children ill, so schools avoid them | Schools sell nuts to children | Nuts are free to take home
exam: Which word is a noun? | Salty | *Cashew | Roasted | Crunchy
